Create a pixel art object with transparent background. ~30-90s. Returns object ID immediately.

Two modes:
- Basic (no background_image): standalone object from description. Requires width/height.
- Style matching (with background_image): matches your map's art style. Width/height auto-detected.
  Default inpainting: oval 60%. Options: oval, rectangle, or custom mask.

Canvas: 32-400px. Basic max 400x400, inpainting max 192x192.
background_image: {"type": "base64", "base64": "..."} (file paths not supported)
inpainting: {"type": "oval", "fraction": 0.3} | {"type": "rectangle", "fraction": 0.5} | {"type": "mask", "mask_image": "base64..."}

Use get_map_object to check status. The object is permanent and can be
placed on a map with place_map_object.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__pixellab__create_map_object(args: {
  // Background image for style matching (optional). Format: {"type": "base64", "base64": "..."}. File paths are not supported (server cannot read local files). If provided without inpainting config, uses default: oval 60%.
  background_image?: string | null;
  // Object description (e.g., 'wooden barrel', 'stone fountain')
  description: string;
  // Detail level
  detail?: "low detail" | "medium detail" | "high detail";
  // Canvas height in pixels (required for basic mode, auto-detected from background_image if provided)
  height?: number | null;
  // Inpainting configuration as JSON string (optional). DEFAULT: If background_image provided but this omitted, uses oval 0.6. Options: {"type": "oval", "fraction": 0.3} for auto oval mask, {"type": "rectangle", "fraction": 0.5} for auto rectangle mask, {"type": "mask", "mask_image": "base64..."} for custom mask. Mask convention: WHITE (255) = area where AI generates, BLACK (0) = frozen/preserved context. Fraction is 0.05-0.95 (how much of background the shape covers).
  inpainting?: string | null;
  // Outline style
  outline?: "single color outline" | "selective outline" | "lineless";
  // Shading complexity
  shading?: "flat shading" | "basic shading" | "medium shading" | "detailed shading";
  // Camera angle
  view?: "low top-down" | "high top-down" | "side";
  // Canvas width in pixels (required for basic mode, auto-detected from background_image if provided)
  width?: number | null;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
